{"repositoryId":277307518,"availability":"available","full":"danielearwicker/flowerbi","name":"flowerbi","description":"Ultra-minimal BI analytics query and UI tools","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":10,"forks":5,"created":"2020-07-05T13:28:18Z","updated":"2026-10-08T16:47:33Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://earwicker.com/flowerbi/demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.580Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.580Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.580Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.580Z","stars":10,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["FlowerBI supports querying relational databases through a single POST route, so that clients have enough power to do aggregation and joins, but the server/API can can carefully limit what clients are able to do.","It focuses on supporting very succinct query definitions at the client, and strong-typing via TypeScript inference.","The Playground lets you interactively build a query, see what the JS/TS code for that query would look like, and also the generated SQL, and the tabulated results."],"features":["in SQL Server databases,","arranged in a star schema,","served up by our own API (dotnet core/C#),","subject to fine-grained row-level authorisation (that is, only some users are allowed to see some rows).","written in TypeScript/React,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/danielearwicker/flowerbi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"feac64be451ae001a9fbbfe0b80f4322bfd74abcf013ad9e8ccc39d16cf21b06","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.691Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:14.691Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"FlowerBI supports querying relational databases through a single POST route, so that clients have enough power to do aggregation and joins, but the server/API can can carefully limit what clients are able to do.","sourceUrl":"https://githu